    "issue_alignment": "PoC is a BGZF-compressed BCF v2.2 file whose single record declares a short shared section (shared_len=31, 7 bytes of shared data) so the INFO key is the final field: ID/REF/ALT/FILTER decode cleanly, then the INFO key typed int has type nibble 3 (INT32) with only 2 value bytes remaining before 'end'. bcf_dec_typed_int1_safe()'s check 'end - p < bcf_type_shift[t]' uses the shift value 2 instead of the 4-byte width, passes, and le_to_i32(p) reads 4 bytes, over-reading 2 bytes past the end of the shared section."
